  "name": "Selleasy",
  "why": "Selleasy is in our dossiers too and solves the same problem with a different meter: when we read it on 19 September 2026 it charged a share of the sales it helped make, 3% on direct sales, 1% on assisted sales and 5% on upsells and cross-sells, with no subscription. Assortion charges a fixed monthly price set by your total orders, from $9.99. If upsells drive a lot of revenue per order, a flat fee is easier to predict; if they sell little, a revenue share costs less."
